.TH "GIT\-STACK" "1" "" "git\-stack" "Git Stack Manual"
.SH NAME
git\-stack \- stacked branches that survive squash merges
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]git stack\f[R] [\f[B]\-C\f[R] \f[I]path\f[R]] \f[I]command\f[R]
[\f[I]args\f[R]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Stacked pull requests on GitHub (or any git host) without the conflicts
that squash merges cause.
It\(aqs a command\-line tool with nothing to sign up for: it keeps what
it knows in your repository\(aqs git config.
.SH QUICK START
.IP
.EX
pipx install git+https://github.com/benekastah/git\-stack   \f[I]# see Install for uv and requirements\f[R]

git switch main
git stack branch add\-api        \f[I]# a branch for PR 1\f[R]
\f[I]# ...commit...\f[R]
git stack branch use\-api        \f[I]# a branch for PR 2, built on PR 1\f[R]
\f[I]# ...commit...\f[R]
git stack push                  \f[I]# push both, and print links to open their PRs\f[R]
.EE
.PP
After that, day to day:
.IP
.EX
git stack sync                  \f[I]# catch up: drop merged PRs, rebase what\(aqs left\f[R]
git stack push                  \f[I]# update the PRs\f[R]
.EE
